  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "Evidence: All four completed experiments use avgpool aggregation, so the effect of aggregation is entirely unexplored. The current best (config_036: pca_n2000 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.639) gives a strong baseline. config_013 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding the best-performing RNA encoder (pca_n2000), image encoder (resnet50), fusion (weighted), and profile setting (multiprofile) constant. This isolates the aggregation effect cleanly. Question tested: Does transformer-based aggregation of multiprofile representations improve over simple average pooling? Why this is the best next experiment: Aggregation is a fundamental architectural choice that has zero coverage in the experiment history, and it is a high-leverage design decision—if transformer aggregation helps, it opens a new optimization axis; if it does not, we confirm avgpool sufficiency and can redirect budget toward RNA encoder or profile-setting variations. It is a single-variable change from the current best, maximizing information per experiment under the limited budget."
}

